FerrionOS change to the Redox kernel (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit e7f1d4231d0f4b55fbef229d9cd9459302c101f4 with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied:
- a futex word in private memory (`Provider::Allocated`) is keyed by its address space and virtual address instead of its physical address. A thread already waiting when another thread of its process forks is then still woken: the waker's first write after the fork breaks copy-on-write and moves the word to a new frame, which left the waiter keyed by the old frame forever. Futexes in memory shared between address spaces stay keyed by physical address.

